# Where each setting comes from. Rows are layers, lowest priority first; "." = unset.
title:   Which setting wins: four config layers, in order of precedence
caption: idle-compact reads its settings from four places. Each row below overrides the rows above it, one setting at a time, and the bottom row is what the mod ends up using.
note:    An example. Here the project file slows the timer to 15 minutes, then a live change in this session asks for 5 minutes and a dry run.

fields  enabled  idleSeconds  minTokens  dryRun  announce
layer  defaults — built into the mod                     mute  true  1200  120000  false  log,toast,notify
layer  plugin options — /config or settings.json        sky   .     .     .       .      log,toast
layer  project file — .claude/idle-compact.json         sand  .     900   150000  .      .
layer  live changes — the config tool, per user         plum  .     300   .       true   .
result  in effect — what the timer uses
